'FilesMetadata'));\ndebug(Inflector::pluralize('Metadata'));\ndebug(Inflector::pluralize('FilesMetadata'));\n/src/Controller/DMSController.php (line 127)\n'Metadata'\n/src/Controller/DMSController.php (line 128)\n'FilesMetadatum' // Expected: FilesMetadata\n/src/Controller/DMSController.php (line 129)\n'Metadata'\n/src/Controller/DMSController.php (line 130)\n'FilesMetadatas' // Expected: FilesMetadata\n```\n\nProblem snowballs to:\n\n``` php\ndebug($this->FilesMetadata);\ndebug($this->Metadata);\n\n/src/Controller/DMSController.php (line 125)\nobject(Cake\\ORM\\Table) { // Failed here\n\n    'table' => 'files_metadata',\n    'alias' => 'FilesMetadata',\n    'entityClass' => '\\Cake\\ORM\\Entity', // Failed here too\n    'associations' => [],\n    'behaviors' => [],\n    'defaultConnection' => 'default',\n    'connectionName' => 'default'\n\n}\n/src/Controller/DMSController.php (line 126)\nobject(App\\Model\\Table\\MetadataTable) {\n\n    'table' => 'metadata',\n    'alias' => 'Metadata',\n    'entityClass' => 'App\\Model\\Entity\\Metadata',\n    'associations' => [\n        (int) 0 => 'collections',\n        (int) 1 => 'files',\n        (int) 2 => 'collectionsmetadata'\n    ],\n    'behaviors' => [],\n    'defaultConnection' => 'default',\n    'connectionName' => 'default'\n\n}\n```\n\nInflector.php > line 32 `$_plural['rules']` > adding: `'/(m)etadata$/i' => '\\1etadata',`\nAdding this line prevents metadata turning into metadatas (but I have no idea on how, just followed the pattern of the code above)\nInflector.php > line 144 `'/([ti])a$/i' => '\\1um',` \nThis line is the rule that transforms FileMetadata into FilesMetadatum\n\nI would submit a PR if I could understand better this rules, but I'm really not confident about it so I tried to point out where the problem is.\n","closed_by":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m